# Agent Workspace — Mandatory Load Protocol

Before executing **any** task in this repository, follow this protocol completely. No step may be skipped.

## 0. Project status log (Required — first read)

Read **`docs/logs/PROJECT_STATUS.md`** for what is **done**, **not done**, and **next**. This overrides stale session logs (e.g. old Supabase blockers). Update that file after every completed task. See **`.cursor/rules/project-status-log.mdc`**.

## 1. Load Context (Required)

Read these files in order:

1. `context/project-overview.md`
2. `context/architecture.md`
3. `context/tech-stack.md`
4. `context/coding-standards.md`

If any file is missing or clearly stale, **stop** and run the **`repository-analyzer`** skill (`.cursor/skills/repository-analyzer/SKILL.md`) before proceeding.

## 2. Load Memory (Required)

Scan before coding:

- `.ai-memory/decisions.md`
- `.ai-memory/architecture-decisions.md`
- `.ai-memory/lessons-learned.md`
- `.ai-memory/agent-notes.md` (for in-progress handoffs)

## 3. Load Orchestration (Required)

Read `AGENTS.md` at repo root for:

- Task → agent delegation matrix
- Skill trigger conditions
- Parallel agent boundaries
- Self-documentation requirements

Identify the **primary agent** for the current task from `agents/*.md`.

## 4. Activate Skills

Load relevant skills from `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`:

| Situation | Skill |
|-----------|-------|
| New workspace / repo changed / context missing | `repository-analyzer` |
| New feature | `feature-builder` |
| API or external integration | `api-integration` |
| Bug or error | `bug-investigator` |
| Refactor | `refactor-assistant` |
| Tests or QA | `test-generator` |
| After any completed work | `documentation-writer` |

## 5. Execution Rules

- **Plan before code** — outline steps and file boundaries.
- **Minimal scope** — do not modify unrelated modules.
- **Follow architecture** — route groups, Supabase RLS, revalidatePath, design system.
- **Verify** — lint/build evidence before claiming done.
- **Commit** — only when user explicitly requests.

## 6. Post-Task (Required)

After every feature or modification:

1. Run **`documentation-writer`** skill
2. Update affected `context/*.md` files
3. Append `.ai-memory/` (decisions, lessons, or agent-notes)
4. Update committed docs/README only when user requests

## 7. Parallel Agents

When work spans frontend + backend + testing:

- Project Manager (`agents/project-manager.md`) coordinates
- Respect file boundaries in `AGENTS.md`
- Log handoffs in `.ai-memory/agent-notes.md`

## Coexistence With Other Rules

This rule **supplements** (does not replace):

- `.cursor/rules/design-system.mdc` — UI changes
- User rules — git safety, commit policy, prose standards
- Installed Cursor plugin skills — use when task-specific; still load context first

**Context and memory load always come first.**
